## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to design an end-to-end, event-driven AWS workflow that combines storage, NLP classification, and structured indexing. It emphasizes practical decisions about ordering, retries, and privacy controls for handling real customer data.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven architecture with S3 and Lambda
- Amazon Comprehend for text classification and named entity recognition (NER)
- Output consolidation and DynamoDB indexing
- IAM least privilege, KMS encryption, and data privacy best practices

## Code Example

```javascript
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  // 1. Get S3 object
  const s3Object = await s3.getObject({
    Bucket: event.bucket,
    Key: event.key
  }).promise();

  const ticket = JSON.parse(s3Object.Body);

  // 2. Validate schema
  if (!ticket.ticketId || !ticket.text) {
    throw new Error('Invalid ticket schema');
  }

  // 3. Classify with Comprehend
  const classifyResult = await comprehend.classifyDocument({
    Text: ticket.text,
    EndpointArn: COMPREHEND_ENDPOINT
  }).promise();

  // 4. Extract entities
  const entitiesResult = await comprehend.detectEntities({
    Text: ticket.text,
    LanguageCode: 'en'
  }).promise();

  const topEntities = entitiesResult.Entities
    .sort((a, b) => b.Score - a.Score)
    .slice(0, 3);

  // 5. Store results in S3 (encrypted)
  const output = {
    ticketId: ticket.ticketId,
    category: classifyResult.Classes[0].Name,
    confidence: classifyResult.Classes[0].Score,
    entities: topEntities,
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString()
  };

  await s3.putObject({
    Bucket: OUTPUT_BUCKET,
    Key: `results/${ticket.ticketId}.json`,
    Body: JSON.stringify(output),
    ServerSideEncryption: 'aws:kms'
  }).promise();

  // 6. Upsert DynamoDB
  await dynamoDB.put({
    TableName: TICKETS_TABLE,
    Item: {
      ticketId: ticket.ticketId,
      s3Key: `results/${ticket.ticketId}.json`,
      category: output.category,
      confidence: output.confidence,
      entities: topEntities
    }
  }).promise();

  return { statusCode: 200, body: 'Success' };
};
```

## Architecture Considerations

| Component | Consideration |
|-----------|----------------|
| **S3 Trigger** | Use S3 Event Notifications to trigger Lambda on object creation |
| **Lambda** | Configure timeout (30s+), memory (512MB+), and VPC if needed |
| **IAM** | Least privilege: Lambda needs read on input bucket, write on output bucket, Comprehend and DynamoDB access |
| **Encryption** | Use SSE-KMS for S3 buckets; enable at-rest encryption for DynamoDB |
| **Error Handling** | Implement DLQ for failed processing; add try-catch with exponential backoff for API calls |
| **Cost** | Comprehend pricing is per request; consider batching if high volume |
| **Privacy** | Never log PII; use AWS PrivateLink for Comprehend if required |

## Why This Is Asked

Tests orchestration, edge cases, and cost/privacy trade-offs for multi-service AWS AI pipelines.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven orchestration (S3 → Step Functions)
- Language detection, sentiment/abuse scoring, translation
- PII redaction and data privacy controls
- Idempotency, retries, and error handling
- Observability (CloudWatch, X-Ray, EventBridge) and cost governance

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Comment": "Chatlog ML pipeline",
  "StartAt": "DetectLanguage",
  "States": {
    "DetectLanguage": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::comprehend:batchDetectDominantLanguage",
      "Parameters": {
        "TextList.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value.messages[*].content"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.languageDetection",
      "Next": "SentimentAnalysis"
    },
    "SentimentAnalysis": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::sagemaker:invokeEndpoint",
      "Parameters": {
        "EndpointName": "chatbot-sentiment-abuse-endpoint",
        "Body.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[*]"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.sentimentAbuse",
      "Next": "TranslationCheck"
    },
    "TranslationCheck": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [{
        "Variable": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[0].DominantLanguage.Code",
        "StringEquals": "en",
        "Next": "PIIRedaction"
      }],
      "Default": "Translation"
    },
    "Translation": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::translate:translateText",
      "Parameters": {
        "Text.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[*].Text",
        "SourceLanguageCode.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[0].DominantLanguage.Code",
        "TargetLanguageCode": "en"
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.translation",
      "Next": "PIIRedaction"
    },
    "PIIRedaction": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "redact-pii-function",
        "Payload": {
          "text.$": "$.translation.TranslatedText ?? $$.Map.Item.Value.messages[*].content",
          "piiTypes": ["EMAIL", "PHONE", "NAME", "CREDIT_CARD"]
        }
      },
      "ResultPath": "$.redacted",
      "Next": "PersistResults"
    },
    "PersistResults": {
      "Type": "Parallel",
      "Branches": [
        {
          "StartAt": "WriteToDataLake",
          "States": {
            "WriteToDataLake": {
              "Type": "Task",
              "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
              "Parameters": {
                "FunctionName": "write-ndjson-function",
                "Payload": {
                  "conversationId.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value.conversationId",
                  "originalContent.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value.messages[*].content",
                  "translatedContent.$": "$.translation.TranslatedText",
                  "language.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[0].DominantLanguage.Code",
                  "sentiment.$": "$.sentimentAbuse.Body.sentiment",
                  "abuseFlag.$": "$.sentimentAbuse.Body.abuse_score > 0.7",
                  "redactedContent.$": "$.redacted.Payload.redactedText"
                }
              },
              "End": true
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "StartAt": "UpdateDynamoDB",
          "States": {
            "UpdateDynamoDB": {
              "Type": "Task",
              "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::dynamodb:updateItem",
              "Parameters": {
                "TableName": "chatbot-conversations-index",
                "Key": {
                  "conversationId": {"S.$": "$$.Map.Item.Value.conversationId"}
                },
                "UpdateExpression": "SET translatedKey = :tk, language = :lang, sentiment = :sent, abuseFlag = :abuse, lastProcessed = :ts",
                "ExpressionAttributeValues": {
                  ":tk": {"S.$": "$.translation.TranslatedText"},
                  ":lang": {"S.$": "$.languageDetection.ResultList[0].DominantLanguage.Code"},
                  ":sent": {"S.$": "$.sentimentAbuse.Body.sentiment"},
                  ":abuse": {"BOOL.$": "$.sentimentAbuse.Body.abuse_score > 0.7"},
                  ":ts": {"S.$": "$$.State.EnteredTime"}
                }
              },
              "End": true
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "Next": "Success"
    },
    "Success": {
      "Type": "Succeed"
    }
  }
}
```

